const v16ReadA={id:"v16-read-a",kind:"passage",label:"Passage for Items 69-72",title:"Neighborhood Cooling Survey",description:"Heat has become a growing public health concern in the city, where afternoon temperatures during the dry season regularly exceed the levels at which heat illness becomes likely. Older adults, young children, and outdoor workers are at greatest risk, and many of them spend time at bus stops, playgrounds, and health centers.\n\nA city mapped afternoon temperatures at bus stops, playgrounds, and health centers.\n\nField teams found, for example, that a playground surrounded by trees could still be hot because its rubber matting absorbed heat and the surrounding walls blocked the breeze. A bus stop with little shade, by contrast, stayed cooler than expected because it faced open ground.\n\nThe hottest points were not always the places with the fewest trees; some had dark roofs, wide pavement, and little airflow. Planners first proposed planting only, but field teams also measured shade duration and surface materials. The revised program combined trees, light-colored roofs, drinking water, and shaded seating. Sensors later showed lower surface temperatures at treated sites, though planners warned that short monitoring could not establish how the measures would perform through every season.",alt:"Passage about heat mapping that found multiple heat causes, led to combined cooling measures, and produced lower short-term surface temperatures without proving year-round performance."};
const v16ReadB={id:"v16-read-b",kind:"passage",label:"Babasahin para sa Aytem 73-76",title:"Lalagyang Muling Ginagamit",description:"Tambak ang plastik na lalagyan at supot na itinatapon araw-araw mula sa pamilihang bayan, at bumabara ang ilan sa mga kanal tuwing umuulan. Hinikayat ng pamunuan ang paggamit ng matibay na lalagyan na maaaring hugasan at gamitin muli.\n\nSinubukan ng pamilihang bayan ang programang maaaring humiram ng matibay na lalagyan ang mamimili kapalit ng maliit na deposito.\n\nIniuwi ng ilang mamimili ang lalagyan at itinabi na lamang sa bahay, habang ang iba ay nagbalik nito sa tindahang pinagbilhan, na walang lugar para dito. Nagsimulang mangamba ang pamunuan na mauubos ang mga lalagyan bago matapos ang pagsubok.\n\nMarami ang gumamit sa unang linggo, ngunit kakaunti ang nagsauli dahil hindi malinaw kung saan ibabalik ang lalagyan. Naglagay ang pamunuan ng mga palatandaan sa bawat labasan, nagbukas ng tatlong return station, at ipinakita sa resibo ang halaga at paraan ng pagbabalik. Tumaas ang porsiyento ng pagsasauli. Gayunman, hiwalay na sinuri ang kalinisan ng hinugasang lalagyan; hindi sapat ang mataas na return rate upang patunayang ligtas itong gamitin muli.",alt:"Teksto tungkol sa programang deposito para sa reusable containers, problemang dulot ng hindi malinaw na balikang lugar, pagdagdag ng return stations at impormasyon, at hiwalay na pagsusuri sa kalinisan."};
const v16ReadC={id:"v16-read-c",kind:"passage",label:"Passage for Items 77-80",title:"Records Retention Review",description:"Government offices are required to keep records that document decisions, transactions, and rights, but not every file needs to be kept forever. The regional office had scanned its paper files over several years, and staff had grown used to saving every version of every document.\n\nA regional office stored nearly every scanned document indefinitely.\n\nStaff described searching for an approved memo and finding a dozen drafts with nearly identical names. Auditors had also asked which version was official, and the office could not always answer with confidence.\n\nSearch became slower, storage costs rose, and staff could not easily distinguish official records from temporary working copies. A review team classified records by legal, administrative, and historical value, then assigned retention periods and documented disposal approval. It also required holds for records connected to audits or pending cases. Storage use declined after duplicate working files were removed, but official records remained traceable through an index and disposal log.",alt:"Passage about classifying digital records, assigning retention periods, preserving audit or case holds, removing duplicate working files, and maintaining traceability through indexes and disposal logs."};
